    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493313572/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Thursday, Sept. 19, 1907
Paris.
Saw the glorious Van Dyck Lady with stars and pink parasol from the Cataneo collection of Genoa. Knoedler is asking a hundred thousand pounds for it!
Hutchins lunched with us, and he and I drove to look for a patent ear-drum for Karin. He was dreadfully indiscreet and told me Algar had been in love with me, but thought I had firmly but kindly turned him down. I was utterly unaware of the whole thing."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 284 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

